{
  "abstract": "Every graph on n vertices with floor(n^2/4)+1 edges contains, for each 3 <= k <= n, a subgraph on k vertices with floor(k^2/4)+1 edges. For k = 3 this is Mantel's theorem. Dirac (1963) and Erdős (1964) proved it independently. It is the case l = floor(k^2/4)+1 of Erdős Problem 766, on the least number of edges f(n;k,l) that forces a k-vertex subgraph with l edges.",
